Result family 210 in openai/math (commit adc7f12): Foulkes' conjecture for sixth powers and quadratic stabilization

Discipline: Algebra.

Formalized: the catalogue records a Lean formalization for this result family (comparator challenge statements). Jasmine has not compiled or checked the proof.

Also listed as: Foulkes’ conjecture for sixth powers and quadratic stabilization.

Summary: Proves the sixth case of Foulkes’ conjecture: $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^bV)$ embeds equivariantly in $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6V)$ for every b ≥ 6 and finite-dimensional complex V. More generally, the canonical multiplication map $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^aV)	o\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^bV)$ is surjective for a ≥ 2 and $b\ge a(a-1)$, giving dimension-independent quadratic stabilization.

Manuscript “Foulkes' conjecture for the sixth symmetric power” (September 25, 2026), not formalized. Abstract: We prove the sixth-symmetric-power case of Foulkes' conjecture. For every integer b ≥ 6 and every finite-dimensional complex vector space V, there is a $\mathop{\mathrm{GL}}
olimits (V)$-equivariant injection $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b V)\hookrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^6 V)$. PDF: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Foulkes-Conjecture-for-the-Sixth-Symmetric-Power-September-25-2026/main.pdf

Manuscript “Quadratic stabilization of the canonical Foulkes--Howe map” (September 25, 2026), formalized. Abstract: For every finite-dimensional complex vector space V, we prove that the canonical Foulkes–Howe map $\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a V)\longrightarrow\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^a(\mathop{\mathrm{Sym}}
olimits ^b V)$ is surjective whenever a ≥ 2 and $b\ge a(a-1)$. This gives a quadratic stabilization bound independent of $\dim V$. PDF: https://github.com/openai/math/blob/adc7f1241b42e322a6451854ab7e4b4c146bf78a/preprints/Quadratic-Stabilization-of-the-Canonical-Foulkes-Howe-Map-September-25-2026/paper.pdf

Formal scope: The formalized result proves surjectivity of the canonical averaged Foulkes–Howe map $\mathrm{Sym}^b(\mathrm{Sym}^a\,V)	o\mathrm{Sym}^a(\mathrm{Sym}^b\,V)$ for every finite-dimensional complex vector space, $a\ge2$, and $b\ge a(a-1)$. It also covers the bijective $a=1$ case, the vanishing-on-products consequence, and the corresponding equivariant embedding in the reverse direction. The sixth-power specialization is covered for $b\ge30$; the companion's full range $b\ge6$ is not included.

Lean theorems: OAI.Problem346.canonical_foulkes_howe_surjective (Quadratic stabilization of the canonical Foulkes–Howe map).
